1. DEFINITIONS

"Project" means the VIR/VOS materials distributed from the official project repository under this license.

"Toolchain Source" means the compiler, parser, lexer, semantic analyzer, optimizer, IR, backends, container writer, headers, build-system source, browser compiler source, and build scripts used to create or compile VOS programs. This includes, without limitation, files under src/, include/, browser/vos-compiler.*, browser/vos-compiler-core.c, CMakeLists.txt, and the platform build scripts.

"Compiler Binary" means any executable, shared library, WebAssembly compiler module, or other compiled form of the Toolchain Source, including vos, vos.exe, vosc, vosc.exe, vosbuild, vosbuild.exe, or a substantially equivalent compiler/toolchain binary.

"Runtime Components" means the VOS execution runtime and support files used to run a Built OS, including vos-runtime.js and cpu-worker.js.

"Built OS" means an operating system, application image, or other end product created by compiling your own or modified VOS source with the Project. A Built OS may include generated .vxe, .vimg, .vhw, .vlib, .vdbg, manifest, symbol, JavaScript, WebAssembly, machine-code, HTML, and Runtime Component files required to execute that Built OS.

2. PERMISSION TO USE

Subject to this license, you may:

(a) download and inspect the Project;
(b) make private copies of the Project;
(c) privately modify the Toolchain Source;
(d) compile the Toolchain Source for your own use;
(e) use the resulting compiler/toolchain to build VOS projects and operating systems;
(f) publicly or privately distribute, publish, sell, or otherwise provide a Built OS that you created; and
(g) include Runtime Components with a Built OS when those Runtime Components are reasonably necessary to run that Built OS.

3. PUBLIC REDISTRIBUTION RESTRICTIONS

Except for a Built OS as permitted by Section 2, you may not publicly redistribute, republish, mirror, repackage, sublicense, sell, or otherwise make available:

(a) the Toolchain Source, whether modified or unmodified;
(b) a Compiler Binary;
(c) standalone Runtime Components outside a Built OS;
(d) a repository, archive, package, installer, SDK, or download whose purpose is to redistribute the Project's compiler/toolchain or build materials; or
(e) a substantially equivalent copy or derivative of the Toolchain Source intended to replace or redistribute the official toolchain.

You may link to the official Project repository or official Project downloads instead of republishing the restricted materials.

4. BUILT OS DISTRIBUTION

You own your original VOS source and original Built OS content, subject to any rights in third-party materials you use.

You may publish a Built OS without publishing the Toolchain Source or Compiler Binary used to build it. You may include generated build products and the Runtime Components necessary to execute that Built OS.

This permission does not grant the right to present the VOS compiler/toolchain itself as part of your own SDK, compiler distribution, or public source package.

5. OFFICIAL-REPOSITORY CONTRIBUTIONS

You may submit patches, pull requests, issues, or other contributions directly to the official Project repository. This limited permission does not authorize maintaining or publishing a separate public mirror or fork containing restricted Toolchain Source except to the extent a hosting platform temporarily creates technical copies necessary to submit a contribution to the official repository.

6. NO TRADEMARK LICENSE

This license does not grant permission to use project names, logos, or marks in a way that implies endorsement, sponsorship, or that an unofficial build is the official VIR/VOS distribution.

7. TERMINATION

Your permissions under this license terminate automatically if you materially violate its terms. If the violation is curable, permissions may be restored by ceasing the violation and removing unauthorized public copies, unless the copyright holder gives written notice otherwise.

